{"resourceIdentifier":"5210","resourceName":"Panzhou County Chicken Farm Manure Composting Project","description":"Panzhou County Chicken Farm Manure Composting Project (hereafter referred to as “the project”) introduces the aerobic composting system to treat chicken manure from Good Luck Farm of the Panzhou County Layer Chicken Farming Project in Xuzhai village, Yangchang township, Panzhou county, Liupanshui city, Guizhou province, China, which is invested and owned by Guizhou Hanwei Egg Industry Co., Ltd. (hereafter referred to as “the project proponent” or “the PP”).  The Good Luck Farm farms 900,000 laying chickens when fully operates. The project is designed to avoid methane emissions through controlled aerobic treatment by composting chicken manure.\r\nLeaving all chicken manure to decay in uncovered anaerobic lagoons within the project boundary is the most likely baseline scenario in the absence of the project activity, in which case methane will be directly emitted to the atmosphere.\r\nThe project was put into operation on 05-January-2023. To collect and aerobically treat the chicken manure from the farm and produce organic fertilizer, the project introduces a mechanical manure collection and conveying system, a composting system, and a fertilizer packaging system. It is estimated that 34,492.5 tonnes of chicken manure will be treated every year, and the annual organic fertilizer production is 10,950 tonnes. The produced organic fertilizers will be sold to nearby farmer for soil application.\r\nThe project activity will reduce GHG emissions by introducing controllable microbial technology to aerobically treat chicken manure, replacing the direct methane emissions to the atmosphere from uncovered anaerobic lagoons in the baseline scenario. It is estimated that 35,865 tCO2e emission reductions will be generated annually, and total emission reductions are 358,650 tCO2e during the 10-year fixed crediting period. During the first monitoring period from 05-Jan-2023 to 31-May-2024, the achieved emission reductions are 38,263 tCO2e.","location":{"latitude":25.922961,"longitude":104.844025},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2024-08-21","endExclusive":"2024-09-21","endInclusive":"2024-09-20"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"5210"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Guizhou Province"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Guizhou Hanwei Egg Industry Co., Ltd."},{"type":"string","value":"Guizhou Province, China"},{"type":"string","value":"carbonmanagement@discoveryesco.com"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"5210"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"35865"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Waste handling and disposal"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"AMS-III.D.,AMS-III.F."}]},{"code":"VALIDATOR_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"CTI Certification Co., Ltd."}]},{"code":"PROJECT_REGISTRATION_DATE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"06/04/2025"}]},{"code":"CREDIT_PERIOD_INFO","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1st, 05/01/2023 - 04/01/2033"}]}]}],"documentGroups":[{"code":"VCS_PIPELINE_DOCUMENTS","description":"VCS Pipeline Documents","documents":[{"uri":"https://registry.verra.org/mymodule/ProjectDoc/Project_ViewFile.asp?FileID=117508&IDKEY=k0e98hfalksuf098fnsdalfkjfoijmn4309JLKJFjlaksjfla9f162043532","documentType":"Draft Project Description","documentName":"VCS_PD_PCP_5210_02AUG24.pdf","uploadDate":"2024-08-21T21:27:16.253Z"},{"uri":"https://registry.verra.org/mymodule/ProjectDoc/Project_ViewFile.asp?FileID=116754&IDKEY=n8723kjnf7kjandsaslmdv09887vaksmrmnwqkjoiuanfnfuq0q161003766","documentType":"Listing Representation","docume